e national environment could narrow the margin, but she would need a large polling surprise to contend.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Neal Dunn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 2nd District is an open Republican-held seat after Neal Dunn's retirement, with a partisan lean of about eight points toward the GOP. Austin Rogers won a contested Republican primary and enters the general election with a major financial advantage, having raised over $1 million and benefited from roughly $1.4 million in outside spending, including a U.S. Chamber endorsement. Amanda Green has raised about $348,000 and carries little cash on hand.\n\nNo credible general-election polling exists, so the outlook rests on fundamentals, ratings, and markets. Most expert raters call the seat Safe or Likely Republican, and Polymarket prices Green's chances near 7%. A minor storyline involves questions about Rogers' family residing in Washington, D.C., but nothing suggests a competitive race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1162, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1045, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1006, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0806, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0753, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0679, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0619, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0853, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0683, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0534, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_